From 9379d87f60e480e84bae64f8be0b92d9fecf3154 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 23:10:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(update): Force update review findings [daveey]

- A turn a forced update stopped is no longer silent: prompt_turn turns
  core_update_forced_stop into a visible, retryable failure ("Stopped for a
  forced Hermes update. Send your message again to continue."), with its own
  Desktop error card and gateway-layer error surface.
- running_turns counts live turn leases of the root and every profile home
  under it, and is null (dialog: "could not tell") when a state.db is
  unreadable, never 0. The lease names no surface, so the confirm copy says the
  update stops Desktop and terminal turns and waits for messaging, API and
  scheduled-job turns instead of promising N stopped turns.
- force-request temp file is uuid-named: concurrent writers in one process no
  longer collide.
- Module docstring: a request names no sha and only hermes-sync clears it.
- Desktop ignores a second Force while one is pending.
- Tests: concurrent writes, multi-profile and unreadable counts, both routes
  through the FastAPI app (auth gate, 409 body), the pause_before_turn entry
  path, the forced-stop failure card, the in-flight guard, a failing GET.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
